{"type":"assistant","uuid":"0b280c83-b428-4c40-9708-685f629e371e","session_id":"bf6465ae-46dd-47c7-a3ce-a0c90c2372ca","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"0b280c83-b428-4c40-9708-685f629e371e","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The build was successful. Let me now provide a summary of the changes made.\n","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0}}}
{"type":"assistant","uuid":"6227ded3-d1dc-4090-945c-0c8ed61c9062","session_id":"bf6465ae-46dd-47c7-a3ce-a0c90c2372ca","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"6227ded3-d1dc-4090-945c-0c8ed61c9062","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Build successful.** Let me provide a summary of the fix.\n\n---\n\n## Summary of Changes\n\nThe bug was in **Aegis Password Manager** — during first-time setup (and the later \"set password\" dialog), checking \"show password\" caused the password confirmation field to be **disabled**, which cleared its text. The validation logic then saw an empty confirm field but returned `true` due to the `|| isChecked` condition, letting users bypass password confirmation entirely.\n\n### Files Modified (3 files, 4 locations)\n\n**1. `app/src/main/java/com/beemdevelopment/aegis/helpers/EditTextHelper.java`**\n- Added `setEditTextChars(EditText text, char[] chars)` helper method to restore text after it's been cleared by `setEnabled(false)`.\n\n**2. `app/src/main/java/com/beemdevelopment/aegis/ui/slides/CustomAuthenticatedSlide.java`** (first-time setup wizard)\n- **Checkbox listener**: Save confirm field text *before* `setEnabled(false)` and restore it *after* — so the text persists across enable/disable cycles.\n- **`isPolicyRespected()`**: Removed `|| _checkPasswordVisibility.isChecked()` — passwords must now always match.\n- **`onUserIllegallyRequestedNextPage()`**: Removed `&& !_checkPasswordVisibility.isChecked()` — the error is always shown when passwords don't match.\n\n**3. `app/src/main/java/com/beemdevelopment/aegis/ui/Dialogs.java`** (set password dialog)\n- **Checkbox listener**: Same save/restore pattern for the confirm field text.\n- **OK button handler**: Removed `&& !switchToggleVisibility.isChecked()` — always validate password equality.\n- **TextWatcher**: Removed `|| switchToggleVisibility.isChecked()` — OK button only enables when passwords actually match.\n\n### How it works now\nWhen \"show password\" is checked, the user can see both password fields as plain text. The confirmation field's content is preserved (no longer lost to `setEnabled(false)`), and the equality check always requires both fields to match — regardless of the checkbox state."}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":33112,"output_tokens":456,"cache_read_input_tokens":31680,"total_tokens":33568}}}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","uuid":"974f6f06-a3e0-4cdf-8e0e-e3aee6eb0e06","session_id":"bf6465ae-46dd-47c7-a3ce-a0c90c2372ca","is_error":false,"duration_ms":126190,"duration_api_ms":67583,"num_turns":3,"result":"**Build successful.** Let me provide a summary of the fix.\n\n---\n\n## Summary of Changes\n\nThe bug was in **Aegis Password Manager** — during first-time setup (and the later \"set password\" dialog), checking \"show password\" caused the password confirmation field to be **disabled**, which cleared its text. The validation logic then saw an empty confirm field but returned `true` due to the `|| isChecked` condition, letting users bypass password confirmation entirely.\n\n### Files Modified (3 files, 4 locations)\n\n**1. `app/src/main/java/com/beemdevelopment/aegis/helpers/EditTextHelper.java`**\n- Added `setEditTextChars(EditText text, char[] chars)` helper method to restore text after it's been cleared by `setEnabled(false)`.\n\n**2. `app/src/main/java/com/beemdevelopment/aegis/ui/slides/CustomAuthenticatedSlide.java`** (first-time setup wizard)\n- **Checkbox listener**: Save confirm field text *before* `setEnabled(false)` and restore it *after* — so the text persists across enable/disable cycles.\n- **`isPolicyRespected()`**: Removed `|| _checkPasswordVisibility.isChecked()` — passwords must now always match.\n- **`onUserIllegallyRequestedNextPage()`**: Removed `&& !_checkPasswordVisibility.isChecked()` — the error is always shown when passwords don't match.\n\n**3. `app/src/main/java/com/beemdevelopment/aegis/ui/Dialogs.java`** (set password dialog)\n- **Checkbox listener**: Same save/restore pattern for the confirm field text.\n- **OK button handler**: Removed `&& !switchToggleVisibility.isChecked()` — always validate password equality.\n- **TextWatcher**: Removed `|| switchToggleVisibility.isChecked()` — OK button only enables when passwords actually match.\n\n### How it works now\nWhen \"show password\" is checked, the user can see both password fields as plain text. The confirmation field's content is preserved (no longer lost to `setEnabled(false)`), and the equality check always requires both fields to match — regardless of the checkbox state.","usage":{"input_tokens":478586,"output_tokens":9071,"cache_read_input_tokens":403392,"total_tokens":487657},"permission_denials":[]}
